{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances","id":466726,"title":"Beneficial durances","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T17:40:49-07:00","id":466726,"title":"Beneficial durances","content":"I'll take as an example a Keeper who abducts a woman in her late teens/early twenties with some sort of eating disorder. He/she/it/whatever then feeds the victim into morbid obesity, and leaves the unfortunate person near a stream, barely able to roll over. The luckless test subject has no food, and getting needed water involves heavy exercise. Over time, the former toy loses weight, and once able to move decently well, gets approached by the local changelings. They're not loyalists, since the Keeper isn't the sort to engender loyalty, or even care about it. Basically, it performs decidedly sadistic experiments on its subjects. Eating disorders, endocrine malfunctions, it applies bizarre treatments, observes the effects, then dumps the subject at the end of the experiment. The subjects have since created a society in the forest, living in the trees, hunting and foraging on the ground, doing their best to stay away from the Keeper's &quot;dogs,&quot; which hunt them for carnal purposes. By the end of her experiences, the young woman is fit, toned, slender - and no longer possessed of an eating disorder.<br /> <br /> How common should such Durances be, do you think, in which the abductee actually gains something that is in arguably a benefit? Not worth the price, perhaps, but definitely a benefit, such as no longer having an eating disorder, or an endocrine malfunction being corrected, or the end to some other chronic condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:00:39-07:00","id":466748,"title":"","content":"Whoa, the idea of that Durance totally gives me the creeps. But, to actually answer your question, I imagine it could happen relatively commonly. Arcadia is a land of beauty as much as it is one of madness, and no one walks away unchanged. A character with some sort of internal issue that one of the True Fae inadvertently cures as part of their backstory sounds pretty cool to me, especially if their Fetch still suffers from the malady. Plus it helps complicate their feelings about Arcadia, and complicated feelings make for the best drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:18:53-07:00","id":466761,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's important to note that the Keeper probably doesn't do it for the <i>purpose</i> of curing or helping that particular thing, and that it's incidental. The Keeper does it to help themselves and their own desires, that happening to line up with curing an eating disorder is just that--happenstance. That said, this is all behind the scenes stuff. On the surface it may appear as though they did that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:30:53-07:00","id":466788,"title":"","content":"Or perhaps the Gentry in question does care about curing the conditions. Its desire is to learn about human sicknesses and how to treat them, though not out of compassion or anything similar. To the Gentry in question, this would be something done out of curiosity, for the challenge of it. That people benefit is totally irrelevant. It doesn't even care what happens to its test subjects after they're discarded. Beyond what their reactions to the &quot;dogs&quot; shows about the efficacy of the treatment, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:32:41-07:00","id":466790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=466748#post466748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, the idea of that Durance totally gives me the creeps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. We're dealing with the Gentry, after all. They're all different sorts of creepy. Even the ones that are nice are creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:38:51-07:00","id":466793,"title":"","content":"I have always thought a keeper like the Doctor would be interesting, considering some of the darker things companions end up facing on a regular basis. <br /> of course default changeling is that the keeper is an abuser, and the changeling is an abuse victim. &gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:49:42-07:00","id":466815,"title":"","content":"That's because Ethan Skemp wanted to avoid romanticizing abduction and abuse, and went too far in the other direction - by his own statement. And yes, a Keeper akin to he Doctor would certainly be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:24:27-07:00","id":466874,"title":"","content":"Well if I'm not mistaken, the Autumn Court is full of Changelings who enjoy what they've become... but could do without the slavery part. Generally, being a Changeling gives power to those who are able to regain their minds and escape from their Keepers. The extent of how useful that power is depends on the individual's perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:28:45-07:00","id":466876,"title":"","content":"This is why I loved Winter Masks' descriptions of Dancers, whose Durance-infused grace &quot;lingers with them every minute of the day.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm glad that Skemp didn't shy away from hard topics, but I look forward to CtL's remake because, in it, those topics won't overshadow everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:41:34-07:00","id":466894,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe a durance in which a Changeling's Fetch actually went onto become quite successful in life. When the Changeling returns, they kill the Fetch and take over, thus granting them a beneficial place among mortal society? Of course if the Changeling was a loser before they were taken, it's possible their high society life may crumble within a matter of months, unless their durance conditioned them for such life styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:52:19-07:00","id":466904,"title":"","content":"I once played an Ogre who came out of Arcadia a better person than when he went in. He started out in life as a jerk and a bully; when he was taken by his Keeper he worked with the other captives around him to survive. It was meant to be a &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; scenario but the boys learned that they each had a better chance of surviving if they all looked out for each other. My character led them in the charge to break out of Arcadia. I statted him as the closest thing to a paladin that I could get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T20:25:43-07:00","id":466923,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me. Our species' main survival advantages are intellect and societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:26:10-07:00","id":467296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=466793#post466793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought a keeper like the Doctor would be interesting, considering some of the darker things companions end up facing on a regular basis.<br /> of course default changeling is that the keeper is an abuser, and the changeling is an abuse victim. &gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you implying the Doctor <i>isn't</i> abusive (or at the very least, rather insensitive to the needs of those who travel with him, in a way that leads to trauma for them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:40:35-07:00","id":467531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=467296#post467296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you implying the Doctor <i>isn't</i> abusive (or at the very least, rather insensitive to the needs of those who travel with him, in a way that leads to trauma for them)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've had a few arcs and one shots addressing this very problem, not the least of which is *cough* <i>The God Complex</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:42:22-07:00","id":467785,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the situation given by LadyLens would be a Durance. It seems like a True Fae could use some magic or a pledge and turn the woman into an eating machine for a period of time.<br /> <br /> But there's probably a lot of changelings who, however close their experience came to breaking them, come out of it a stronger person in one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:55:18-07:00","id":467810,"title":"","content":"All durances are beneficial in that they give you access to abilities that no humans have - you get contracts and dreams and pledges and influence over fate and all that, possibly among other things. <br /> <br /> The point is, though - there's always a pretty high price to pay. You pay it by not being the same person you were before they took you away and violated you. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:41:05-07:00","id":467836,"title":"","content":"I fail to see why it wouldn't be Durance, at least in the common meaning. The woman was held against her will and forced to do or submit to things she didn't want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:18:26-07:00","id":467865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=467296#post467296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you implying the Doctor <i>isn't</i> abusive (or at the very least, rather insensitive to the needs of those who travel with him, in a way that leads to trauma for them)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's one episode where they're on mars (<i>I think</i>) and there's some kind of deadly water they're trying to evade. There's a woman who's supposed to die, but the Doctor saves her because he likes her. When she calls him out on it, he says he doesn't care if she was supposed to die. After she goes inside her home, she immediately shoots herself in order to correct the time line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:58:22-07:00","id":467894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=467865#post467865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> There's one episode where they're on mars (<i>I think</i>) and there's some kind of deadly water they're trying to evade. There's a woman who's supposed to die, but the Doctor saves her because he likes her. When she calls him out on it, he says he doesn't care if she was supposed to die. After she goes inside her home, she immediately shoots herself in order to correct the time line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would have been a great episode except for the fact that it is literally never referenced again, including in the episode it directly leads into where it was implied he would face consequences for his actions. Also while an excellent example of the Doctor's hubris, they've never really successfully addressed the fact that the Doctor can be an emotionally abusive manchild. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that I say this as a Whovian, but the Doctor really is not someone I'd want to be friends with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:34:46-07:00","id":467960,"title":"","content":"He's not somebody you want to be enemies with either...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:03:28-07:00","id":468046,"title":"","content":"&quot;It was then we knew why this Doctor, who had fought with gods and demons, had run from us and hid himself. He was being kind.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T22:02:07-07:00","id":468124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=468046#post468046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It was then we knew why this Doctor, who had fought with gods and demons, had run from us and hid himself. He was being kind.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Speaking of Durances... imagine being assigned to do THIS, for decades straight...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2dJOIf4mdus\" data-code=\"2dJOIf4mdus\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2dJOIf4mdus/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T04:09:00-07:00","id":468281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=467894#post467894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would have been a great episode except for the fact that it is literally never referenced again, including in the episode it directly leads into where it was implied he would face consequences for his actions. Also while an excellent example of the Doctor's hubris, they've never really successfully addressed the fact that the Doctor can be an emotionally abusive manchild.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's /alluded to/, if not referenced directly - see the scene in the cafe in &quot;End of Time&quot; where the Doctor talks about thinking it would be better alone and ending up doing some things that went wrong. See also the Doctor's final decision in &quot;End of Time&quot; - it seems like he's going to make the hubristic choice, but this time chooses to accept what's going to happen. It's given power because we've seen him make the hubristic choice in the preceding story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:02:43-07:00","id":468743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=468281#post468281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's /alluded to/, if not referenced directly - see the scene in the cafe in &quot;End of Time&quot; where the Doctor talks about thinking it would be better alone and ending up doing some things that went wrong. See also the Doctor's final decision in &quot;End of Time&quot; - it seems like he's going to make the hubristic choice, but this time chooses to accept what's going to happen. It's given power because we've seen him make the hubristic choice in the preceding story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even more fucked up though is that it's supposed to indicate that Tenth is forced into the insidious death situation thanks to the karma from Waters of Mars.<br /> <br /> Yes, that's what they were doing. I think it's stupid. The entire End of Time was stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:42:51-07:00","id":468947,"title":"","content":"Actually, the beginning of the last <i>Malibu Dream House</i> session was a discussion among the PCs where it was asked IC &quot;Can a durance be a good thing.&quot; Members of the Motley varied in terms of how their durances were (Insincere Marguerite's was a fun adventure for her and Ace's almost idyllicly peaceful, while Calamity's was all emotional abuse and Lorelei was often quite helpless and afraid. ) It's an interesting question. <br /> <br /> I as GM don't require a Durance to be bad, just that the character wanted or needed to return to the mundane world eventually. And even Insincere Marguerite and Ace have fears related to Arcadia...Insincere Marguerite made a lot of Gentry very angry, and sees a path ahead of her where she may turn into the same sort of Gentry who took her, while Ace turned on and attacked his Keeper when he saw him turning another captive into a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T17:09:39-07:00","id":468978,"title":"","content":"One day I want to play a changeling who was taken because of a deal they made with a Stranger that involved being taken away if her home conditions ever got bad or dangerous(the logic of a child can be terrible). The return home now has her wondering if things would have been better or worse for having that happened, particularly some problems with her father turned out to be the result of a brain disease that might have been found out earlier if things went differently. Her relationship with her Keeper is amiable enough as a godmother and goddaughter relationship goes, with her even getting advice and opinions from her, but she won't take up the option to go back until she deals with the mess she made, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Another one is just simply the result of a guy getting an impossible surgery done by the Fae. No malice intended, but time is a bitch, and the Strangers don't give refunds on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T23:42:09-07:00","id":469225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=468743#post468743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more fucked up though is that it's supposed to indicate that Tenth is forced into the insidious death situation thanks to the karma from Waters of Mars.<br /> <br /> Yes, that's what they were doing. I think it's stupid. The entire End of Time was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Eh? No, seriously, eh? He _chose_ that. _We_ might see it as karma, but in setting? It was his choice, in no small part influenced by all the hubristic attempts to fight death he'd seen all around him. There is absolutely nothing in the text that says &quot;this is karma for what Ten did earlier&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:06:34-07:00","id":469565,"title":"","content":"Don't forget there are also Kiths who's positions in Arcadia don't seem all that terrible. True Friends (domestic pets) and Playmates (BFF's), for example were apparently loved and cared for by their Keepers, but ultimately they decided they missed the human world and had to return. Not every Durance is a living nightmare, some can be dreams come true, and some never even want to return, such as Loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:40:48-07:00","id":469580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469225#post469225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Eh? No, seriously, eh? He _chose_ that. _We_ might see it as karma, but in setting? It was his choice, in no small part influenced by all the hubristic attempts to fight death he'd seen all around him. There is absolutely nothing in the text that says &quot;this is karma for what Ten did earlier&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the commentary and behind the scenes stuff on this story. It may never be explicitly said, but that's absolutely the subtext they put in there.<br /> <br /> You know, under the even more blatant subtext of RTD whining like a big baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T14:10:41-07:00","id":469590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469565#post469565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget there are also Kiths who's positions in Arcadia don't seem all that terrible. True Friends (domestic pets) and Playmates (BFF's), for example were apparently loved and cared for by their Keepers, but ultimately they decided they missed the human world and had to return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plausible, but not by default. Truefriends are turned into animals known for providing love, loyalty, and companionship above all else: that says nothing about how their Keepers actually treat them. Playmates, meanwhile, are... well, just taken to give a Stranger someone to play with: that says nothing about the Stranger playing nicely.<br /> <br /> With the way the Gentry are generally depicted... Those Kiths can easily result from cases like a puppy who keeps optimistically crawling forward on broken legs, hopeful that <i>this time</i> its master will return its love; or that cool kid you really want to be friends with keeps forcing you to play the sorts of games that Wednesday and Pugsley Addams would adore, including <i>all</i> the grotesquely horrible violence ( &quot;the good parts,&quot; the cool kid calls them). I'm kinda reminded of a point near the end of Mother 3, when you're forced to play games with someone who loves games, but hates losing; you have to play poorly enough to lose AND well enough for it to have been close. There's no penalty in that game for messing up, other than doing it over, but I could see one of the Gentry getting <i>brutal</i> after losing or being allowed to win. And even those sorts of horrible Durances are likely to still have periods when the slightest bit of affection or praise made them happier than they'd ever been before or since.<br /> <br /> Relatively pleasant Durances are certainly possible -- Wild Sam from Grim Fears, introducing the Playmate Kith, was pretty much this. It's just not the game's assumption for PCs. Even Wild Sam's Durance clearly screwed him up good and proper, though: he's essentially locked into perpetual developmental and physical childhood, his Keeper got bored of him and cast him out, and rejection is <i>really</i> not something he takes well. Whatever Arcadia and the Gentry serve up to visiting mortals, it's very rarely completely healthy. &quot;Beautiful Madness,&quot; remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T18:26:25-07:00","id":469716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469590#post469590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the way the Gentry are generally depicted... Those Kiths can easily result from cases like a puppy who keeps optimistically crawling forward on broken legs, hopeful that <i>this time</i> its master will return its love</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're an a-hole for putting that image in my head! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, its kind of difficult to imagine a completely happy durance when the True Fae are incapable of understanding even the basic concepts of charity, love, compassion, kindness or friendship. They just imitate it as best they're able to interpret.<br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I would have to say the Wizened have the most chance of a beneficial durance. Your durance teaches you a trade skill, talent or craft and thanks to the magic of Arcadia, you're able to perform it with supernatural levels of skill and precision. If you manage to escape, you could get a decent job or even a career! Some might even offer the keys to escape, such as a Brewer having access to their Keeper's drink... which they can spike!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:40:53-07:00","id":469859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469716#post469716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Come to think of it, I would have to say the Wizened have the most chance of a beneficial durance. Your durance teaches you a trade skill, talent or craft and thanks to the magic of Arcadia, you're able to perform it with supernatural levels of skill and precision. If you manage to escape, you could get a decent job or even a career! Some might even offer the keys to escape, such as a Brewer having access to their Keeper's drink... which they can spike!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of a slippery slope as you're basically comparing house-slaves and field-hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:14:57-07:00","id":470108,"title":"","content":"One thing I think needs to be kept always in mind is that the Gentry are not demons or devils. They're alien beings; they do not think as we do, but they're not automatically and reflexively hurtful. Sometimes, they even take the role of the good guy, as best they understand it. The caring doctor, the loving matron, these are archetypes just as valid as any other. Gentry kindness is not human kindness, but neither is Gentry cruelty the same as human cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:40:14-07:00","id":471615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469716#post469716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're an a-hole for putting that image in my head! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here, let me see if I can dispel it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QNot4iC7K8s\" data-code=\"QNot4iC7K8s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QNot4iC7K8s/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T17:51:34-07:00","id":471907,"title":"","content":"Thank you. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, beneficial is a matter of perspective. What one person deems as helpful may not apply to another. Especially if that help comes in the form of tough love, which not everyone could recognize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:26:45-07:00","id":472019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/466726-beneficial-durances?p=469716#post469716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're an a-hole for putting that image in my head! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can actually kinda sympathize, since I'm not sure I dig being the guy who <i>came up with</i> the image. ^_^o There's also a smidgen of, well, meta-discomfort: I feel that mental image should distress me more than it does.<br /> <br /> Many thanks to Daydreamer for running damage control in spectacular fashion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http: